# Milestone: M3
# Covers: 'at (trace.enter?)' and 'at (trace.leave?)' reactive watchers fire
#         on tag entry and exit; works on normal exit, stop, and exception.
# deferred: v1.x — at(tag.enter?)/at(tag.leave?) events not implemented (T55)
# matrix-row: tag-scope-events
#
# Reason:
#   'at (trace.enter?)' and 'at (trace.leave?)' are reactive watchers on tag-
#   event pseudo-events — they require the full M5 reactive runtime (watcher
#   eval loop, event-based firing).  tag.stop() method dispatch is M4.  The
#   fixture also uses ',' for parallel observation (M5 chk driver).  Tag enter/
#   leave event emission is part of the watcher subsystem activation in M5.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5 with reactive runtime and tag events):
# # var trace = Tag.new() | {};
# # at(trace.enter?) echo("enter");
# # at(trace.leave?) echo("leave");
# # trace: echo("Say hi");
# # [00000001] *** enter
# # [00000002] *** Say hi
# # [00000003] *** leave
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/tag/enter-leave.chk)
